            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test demonstrates air leakage on the following house components:

-Windows: All windows

oDouble single panes wood windows 

oVinyl windows located on the rear bedroom, handle broken and doesn?????????t close 

-Door: We noticed air leakage around the back door. 

-Electrical panel: We noticed air leakage around the electrical panel

-Bathrooms ceilings evacuations fans 

The infiltration test showed a very high level of air leakage. We strongly recommend sealing the building by following the recommendations listed in this report. With these results, the energy consumption will be very high and will result arising the cost of heating. Reseal the building will help to reduce the heating cost ad increase the comfort into the living space.

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the moment of the assessment the walls are made by 2x6 with an insulation level estimated of R-19. This level of insulation is far under the actual standard, we recommend using the city of Whitehorse standard of R-28. We recommend, to proceed from the exterior, in this way it will give the possibility to wrap the building and ensure proper air sealing of the building. Also, by working from outside, the addition of insulation will not reduce the interior space and it will also eliminate the unpleasantness of living through renovations. </mainWalls>
                <ceilings>At the time of the inspection we observed that the roof insulation level is R-28. We recommend adding insulation to meet the actual standard of the National Building Code based at R-40. Therefore, we recommend using the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60. More insulation reduces heat loss during the heating season and also reduces the migration of heat inside the living space in the summertime.</ceilings>
                <foundation>At the moment of the inspection, it was impossible to see the insulation of the crawlspace. Unfortunately, the snow covers the entire surface and access to the crawlspace. We estimate the floor to be made by 2x8 with an insulation level of R-28. We recommend the verification of the insulation and the condition of the floor structure. We also recommend the addition of insulation if the level is lower than the one estimated.</foundation>
                <windows>At the moment of the inspection, we noticed that all windows leaks and some are broken. We also notice condensation and frosting on the windows. The majority of the windows are single panes windows but assembled with a second window which it makes as a double window. We recommend the replacement of all windows by triple panes  ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED product and suitable for Canada Zone 3.</windows>
                <doors>We noticed air leakage coming from the back door. The addition of weather strips might help to reduce the gap between the door and the frame. If replacement of the door, we recommend using an ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED product.</doors>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
